1
00:00:05,467 --> 00:00:12,567
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,933
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,433 --> 00:00:46,800
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:57,233
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,767
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,867 --> 00:01:00,900
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,633
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,967 --> 00:01:07,467
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:10,367 --> 00:01:11,967
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,467 --> 00:01:17,367
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,533 --> 00:01:19,600
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,100
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:24,933
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:28,433
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,733 --> 00:01:31,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:35,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,333 --> 00:01:36,167
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,333 --> 00:01:37,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,867 --> 00:01:39,033
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:46,433 --> 00:01:49,167
It's time for us to really sell
<i> Salvador out here.</i>

24
00:01:49,267 --> 00:01:53,167
<i> You will have your own show!</i>

25
00:01:53,267 --> 00:01:56,000
<i>We just need to do
a makeover.</i>

26
00:01:56,100 --> 00:02:00,400
<i>The controversies about the
demolition of Ginintuang Lupa,</i>

27
00:02:00,567 --> 00:02:01,967
<i> I have no fault in that.</i>

28
00:02:02,067 --> 00:02:06,000
<i>I want to pay back the favor
you did for my father.</i>

29
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:08,500
I'm here to give financial aid.

30
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:10,800
<i>If you came here
to buy us off...</i>

31
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:12,167
<i>You can't pay off
my father's hospitalization!</i>

32
00:02:12,267 --> 00:02:13,200
<i> Leave!</i>

33
00:02:13,367 --> 00:02:15,000
<i>What did you do
to the motorcycle?</i>

34
00:02:15,133 --> 00:02:17,567
<i> He was about to pay for it!</i>

35
00:02:17,733 --> 00:02:19,567
<i>We could've used that money
for your father's operation!</i>

36
00:02:19,733 --> 00:02:22,100
<i> Don't worry. I'll get it back.</i>

37
00:02:22,267 --> 00:02:23,233
<i> Use your beauty and charm.</i>

38
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:25,233
<i>Find out where
the motor parts are located.</i>

39
00:02:25,367 --> 00:02:27,700
<i>I was hoping to ask
if you sell parts here.</i>

40
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,067
<i> For motorcycles.</i>

41
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,600
Let's discuss it in our office.

42
00:02:30,767 --> 00:02:32,700
<i> Ah! Ah!</i>

43
00:02:34,267 --> 00:02:35,400
<i> Gabo!</i>

44
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:38,567
<i> Come on, let's go!</i>

45
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:41,033
<i>- They're coming!
- I'll distract them!</i>

46
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:48,533
<i> Ahh!</i>

47
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,767
He said...

48
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:57,733
I will have--

49
00:02:58,267 --> 00:02:59,367
Just me.

50
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:02,400
I'll host my own show.

51
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:06,533
Wow! You're so great!
Oh my, I hope this develops!

52
00:03:06,633 --> 00:03:10,433
You know, luckily,
I never regretted

53
00:03:10,567 --> 00:03:13,400
having you as my partner!
You're so great!

54
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:15,967
- You're so talented!
- Salvador, Oli.

55
00:03:16,133 --> 00:03:19,233
Give another report
against NLEA and Gen. Jacinto.

56
00:03:19,333 --> 00:03:21,400
Okay? The audience loves that!

57
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:24,333
We have to make the most
of that issue, okay?

58
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:26,167
Alright, boss.

59
00:03:26,333 --> 00:03:28,667
We'll find an interviewee
for the report.

60
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:32,100
Go to the place,
so we can feel the setting.

61
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:35,300
Focus on criticizing Jacinto.

62
00:03:35,467 --> 00:03:40,467
Make it hot, feisty,
and, especially, dangerous.

63
00:03:40,633 --> 00:03:42,400
Do it well, alright?

64
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:43,967
[STUTTERING] Wait, Salvador.

65
00:03:45,333 --> 00:03:46,667
I thought you'll be hosting?

66
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:49,067
Why is he still asking you
to do field reports?

67
00:03:49,167 --> 00:03:51,633
Never mind that.
We'll just report.

68
00:03:51,767 --> 00:03:56,133
What matters is I have a job,
and you have a job too.

69
00:03:56,333 --> 00:03:58,467
- That's right, Salvador.
- If you don't irritate me.

70
00:03:58,567 --> 00:04:00,133
- Bingo! Okay.
- Let's go.

71
00:04:00,233 --> 00:04:01,167
Thank you, thank you, Salvador.

72
00:04:02,067 --> 00:04:03,167
[MANNY] Boss?

73
00:04:03,333 --> 00:04:04,500
[CUTLERY CLINKS]

74
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,767
- Engr. Fernandez.
- Engr. Fernandez!

75
00:04:08,867 --> 00:04:11,367
Welcome to my home,
and thank you for your interest.

76
00:04:11,533 --> 00:04:13,467
I came here in a hurry

77
00:04:13,567 --> 00:04:16,300
because I'm very interested
in your project.

78
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:18,133
Nice to hear.
Please, have a seat.

79
00:04:18,233 --> 00:04:19,167
Thank you.

80
00:04:21,367 --> 00:04:23,500
[CHAIR THUDS]

81
00:04:26,467 --> 00:04:30,133
Tell me about your development.
It's Ginintuang Lupa, correct?

82
00:04:30,267 --> 00:04:32,967
Well, let's say,
a development...

83
00:04:33,767 --> 00:04:35,033
- by the sea...
- Mm-hmm.

84
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:37,033
But in the heart of Manila.

85
00:04:37,167 --> 00:04:39,833
I mean, from that alone,
you can see the huge potential.

86
00:04:40,533 --> 00:04:41,633
We're going to make it
a leisure hub,

87
00:04:41,733 --> 00:04:45,533
so we plan to build
casinos, hotels,

88
00:04:45,667 --> 00:04:47,867
condominiums, and malls.

89
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:50,333
And we'll make sure
that it's a...

90
00:04:50,867 --> 00:04:52,200
...must-visit destination.

91
00:04:52,367 --> 00:04:55,367
I'm really looking
to invest my money.

92
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:56,967
Thank you.

93
00:04:57,400 --> 00:05:01,300
- That calls for a drink.
- It seems to early too drink.

94
00:05:01,433 --> 00:05:02,733
Well, Engr. Fernandez, it's...

95
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:05,167
...5 o'clock somewhere
in this world.

96
00:05:05,267 --> 00:05:07,167
[CHUCKLING]

97
00:05:07,267 --> 00:05:08,200
Wait a minute.

98
00:05:12,267 --> 00:05:13,700
Manny, let's give Mr. Gomez

99
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:16,733
- our best whiskey.
- Best whiskey! [CHUCKLES]

100
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:24,867
Well, boss? Is the list
of investors I gave you good?

101
00:05:24,967 --> 00:05:27,167
- You're really dependable.
- Boss, you know,

102
00:05:27,267 --> 00:05:29,767
if Mr. Gomez's money
comes in...

103
00:05:29,933 --> 00:05:32,900
I'm certain we can start
the Phase 1 of the development.

104
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,900
Well, it looks like this is...

105
00:05:35,633 --> 00:05:36,900
...my lucky day.

106
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,600
[CHUCKLING]

107
00:05:40,967 --> 00:05:41,800
<i> -</i> [SALVADOR]<i> Unbelievable!
<i>- Sir.</i></i>

108
00:05:41,967 --> 00:05:43,733
<i>- Harsh suffering was...
- Take a look.</i>

109
00:05:43,833 --> 00:05:45,367
<i>...inflicted on the people
during the demolition</i>

110
00:05:45,467 --> 00:05:46,367
<i> in Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

111
00:05:46,467 --> 00:05:47,600
<i> And I found out</i>

112
00:05:47,767 --> 00:05:50,233
<i> that the owner of the land</i>

113
00:05:50,333 --> 00:05:52,367
<i> is General Ricardo Jacinto!</i>

114
00:05:52,467 --> 00:05:53,800
Is this real?

115
00:05:53,967 --> 00:05:55,967
Looks like we're going
to have a problem.

116
00:05:56,133 --> 00:05:58,933
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

117
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:03,033
I've been saving this bottle
for an occasion just like this.

118
00:06:04,067 --> 00:06:04,933
[CORK POPS]

119
00:06:05,567 --> 00:06:06,933
[ALCOHOL SLOSHING]

120
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:08,100
[BOTTLE THUDS]

121
00:06:09,433 --> 00:06:10,900
Partner!

122
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:15,133
Maybe I should think twice
before calling you that.

123
00:06:15,267 --> 00:06:18,967
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

124
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:21,433
Uh, Engr. Fernandez,
just a while ago,

125
00:06:21,533 --> 00:06:23,133
you were very interested.

126
00:06:23,267 --> 00:06:24,800
I mean, what changed?

127
00:06:27,833 --> 00:06:31,133
<i> General Ricardo Jacinto!</i>

128
00:06:31,267 --> 00:06:34,967
<i>Are you done with the people
from Ginintuang Lupa,</i>

129
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,933
<i> or just cooling off?</i>

130
00:06:38,033 --> 00:06:44,633
<i>You law enforcers act
like you're demigods!</i>

131
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:46,500
<i> Let me spell it out, General,</i>

132
00:06:46,633 --> 00:06:49,167
<i> in case you're slow to grasp.</i>

133
00:06:49,333 --> 00:06:52,167
You behave as if you were gods!

134
00:06:52,333 --> 00:06:54,267
<i> Back when you headed the NLEA,</i>

135
00:06:54,367 --> 00:07:00,700
<i>abusive officers
were everywhere!</i>

136
00:07:00,867 --> 00:07:03,167
<i>Are you truly enforcers
of the law,</i>

137
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:05,167
<i> or just power-trippers...</i>

138
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:08,000
...flexing your muscles?

139
00:07:08,533 --> 00:07:09,967
Is that what you want?
Then face me!

140
00:07:10,067 --> 00:07:12,267
<i>I challenge you!
Want to flaunt your strength?</i>

141
00:07:12,367 --> 00:07:15,933
<i>Think you're strong?
Come on, let's settle this!</i>

142
00:07:16,067 --> 00:07:17,000
<i> Check them out!</i>

143
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,233
This is nothing.

144
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:19,867
Engineer, as you're well aware,

145
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:24,067
issues like this are a normal
part of any project.

146
00:07:24,233 --> 00:07:27,033
How can you pull this off when
that's the sentiment toward you?

147
00:07:27,167 --> 00:07:29,200
He's insulting you straight
to your face!

148
00:07:29,367 --> 00:07:30,467
I can see it now.

149
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:32,667
This business venture will be
one headache after another.

150
00:07:32,933 --> 00:07:35,367
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

151
00:07:35,533 --> 00:07:36,400
[ENGINEER FERNANDEZ]
Thanks, anyway.

152
00:07:36,567 --> 00:07:37,500
Maybe next time.

153
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:41,200
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

154
00:07:43,767 --> 00:07:45,000
- [SLAMS TABLE]
<i> -</i> [SALVADOR] We'll fight back!

155
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:47,033
- Sir...
<i> - General Ricardo--</i>

156
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:49,900
- That reporter just won't quit.
- [SIGHS]

157
00:07:50,033 --> 00:07:52,433
He's provoking us on purpose.

158
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,900
Does he think being part
of the media

159
00:07:54,033 --> 00:07:55,767
gives him the right
to attack us?

160
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:57,600
I know General Jacinto.

161
00:07:57,767 --> 00:07:59,833
If we're already boiling
with anger,

162
00:07:59,933 --> 00:08:02,667
then he's definitely fuming.

163
00:08:02,767 --> 00:08:05,100
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

164
00:08:05,267 --> 00:08:06,167
Sir.

165
00:08:07,033 --> 00:08:09,100
Maybe in this kind of situation,

166
00:08:09,267 --> 00:08:12,233
we can wait for things
to cool down.

167
00:08:12,633 --> 00:08:14,167
This will pass.

168
00:08:14,633 --> 00:08:17,233
That's where
you're wrong, Umali.

169
00:08:17,633 --> 00:08:19,600
General Jacinto is not
that kind of person.

170
00:08:19,767 --> 00:08:23,267
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

171
00:08:23,933 --> 00:08:25,767
Good job! [CHUCKLES]

172
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:27,100
- Could you open it?
- [DOOR SLIDING OPEN]

173
00:08:27,267 --> 00:08:29,067
- Can you handle it?
- Yeah, I can.

174
00:08:29,167 --> 00:08:30,700
[GRUNTING]

175
00:08:31,433 --> 00:08:32,367
[GROANS]

176
00:08:32,467 --> 00:08:33,767
Wow. [CHUCKLES]

177
00:08:33,933 --> 00:08:35,133
You know what, Salvador?

178
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:36,600
Honestly, I'm impressed.

179
00:08:36,767 --> 00:08:38,100
That was gutsy of you.

180
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:39,867
Listen, Oli...

181
00:08:39,967 --> 00:08:42,467
I just can't stand
abusive people.

182
00:08:42,633 --> 00:08:45,767
Besides, the public needs
to see the truth.

183
00:08:45,933 --> 00:08:46,800
[OLI] That's not it.

184
00:08:46,967 --> 00:08:50,267
I think you can feel it now.

185
00:08:50,433 --> 00:08:51,933
Your career is on the rise.

186
00:08:52,067 --> 00:08:53,900
That's why your reporting is
burning with passion.

187
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,133
Forget it.
[CHUCKLES]

188
00:08:55,333 --> 00:08:56,267
Me? Becoming a host?

189
00:08:56,367 --> 00:08:57,267
[LIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

190
00:08:57,367 --> 00:08:58,467
That doesn't even feel real.

191
00:08:58,967 --> 00:09:00,133
Just drop it.

192
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:02,567
Wait, wait. Didn't Boss Arnel
make that promise to you?

193
00:09:03,467 --> 00:09:07,133
With Boss Arnel,
out of ten things he says,

194
00:09:07,300 --> 00:09:09,833
eleven are wrong.
Sometimes even twelve.

195
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,300
There you go again.

196
00:09:11,433 --> 00:09:13,233
You ended up this way

197
00:09:13,333 --> 00:09:15,400
because you've been
in the company for years

198
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:16,633
without recognition.

199
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:20,733
So now you think, why would
they pay attention to you now?

200
00:09:20,833 --> 00:09:22,100
- Right?
- You nailed it.

201
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,233
Of course I did.

202
00:09:23,333 --> 00:09:25,500
Now, hang on.
Let's not forget something.

203
00:09:25,667 --> 00:09:27,067
You followed my advice.

204
00:09:27,167 --> 00:09:30,967
To show off in your reporting
to catch their attention.

205
00:09:31,167 --> 00:09:33,200
That's how you'll get noticed.

206
00:09:33,667 --> 00:09:35,167
Salvador, I'm sure of it.

207
00:09:35,333 --> 00:09:36,000
I'm absolutely sure.

208
00:09:36,167 --> 00:09:37,767
You'll have your own show.

209
00:09:37,867 --> 00:09:41,000
Until it happens,
I won't believe it.

210
00:09:41,167 --> 00:09:42,033
No way.

211
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:44,333
I'm the careful type.
Now, get in.

212
00:09:44,467 --> 00:09:45,633
There you go again. Fine!

213
00:09:45,733 --> 00:09:46,700
- Time to go.
- Let's get going.

214
00:09:46,867 --> 00:09:47,700
[CAR DOOR SLIDING, CLOSES]

215
00:09:47,867 --> 00:09:48,767
[OLI] Let's go, come on!

216
00:09:48,867 --> 00:09:55,967
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

217
00:09:57,900 --> 00:09:59,000
[GLASS THUDS]

218
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,367
[HUFFS]

219
00:10:05,567 --> 00:10:07,300
[LINE RINGING]

220
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:12,367
[PHONE RINGING]

221
00:10:12,833 --> 00:10:14,033
- General Jacinto.
<i> - Domingo.</i>

222
00:10:14,167 --> 00:10:17,867
The Manila Telebalita reporter
is tearing my business apart.

223
00:10:18,033 --> 00:10:19,033
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

224
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,133
He's pushing it way too far.

225
00:10:21,233 --> 00:10:22,067
Yes, sir.

226
00:10:22,233 --> 00:10:24,533
That reporter is a real thorn
in the side.

227
00:10:24,667 --> 00:10:26,233
You know what to do.

228
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:29,033
But Domingo...

229
00:10:30,833 --> 00:10:32,367
you already messed up once.

230
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:33,967
<i>Make sure it doesn't
happen again.</i>

231
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:37,033
I won't mess this up,
General Jacinto.

232
00:10:37,133 --> 00:10:40,167
I'm going to mobilize our men.
You can count--

233
00:10:40,433 --> 00:10:41,333
[PHONE BEEPS]

234
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:42,767
[LINE DROPPED]

235
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:48,233
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

236
00:10:48,367 --> 00:10:49,900
We need to act now.

237
00:10:50,067 --> 00:10:51,667
Round up the henchmen.

238
00:10:51,767 --> 00:10:52,867
What's the plan, sir?

239
00:10:52,967 --> 00:10:55,667
We're going to silence
Salvador's mouth.

240
00:10:55,767 --> 00:10:58,700
Remember, failure is
not an option.

241
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:01,067
Or else, General Jacinto
will have our heads.

242
00:11:01,233 --> 00:11:02,167
Sir.

243
00:11:02,767 --> 00:11:05,233
Paquito and Django are reliable.

244
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:08,733
The next time I speak
with General Jacinto,

245
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:12,433
he must be pleased
with the news I bring him.

246
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:14,533
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir.

247
00:11:14,633 --> 00:11:21,467
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

248
00:11:27,133 --> 00:11:28,600
[ISOBEL] Oh, Ricardo.

249
00:11:29,167 --> 00:11:31,700
I saw Engineer
Fernandez was here.

250
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:34,100
What happened? Were you able
to close the deal?

251
00:11:34,267 --> 00:11:35,900
Did you negotiate with him?

252
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:40,033
- He backed out.
- What?

253
00:11:40,133 --> 00:11:41,567
What did you do?

254
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,967
Remember the reporter
who always has something to say?

255
00:11:44,133 --> 00:11:45,567
Well, Fernandez saw his report.

256
00:11:46,933 --> 00:11:49,067
He got scared
of the negative publicity.

257
00:11:49,867 --> 00:11:51,267
Oh my gosh!

258
00:11:51,967 --> 00:11:55,333
I'm getting worried
about Ginintuang Lupa.

259
00:11:55,467 --> 00:11:57,733
If we sit and don't do anything,

260
00:11:57,833 --> 00:12:00,267
this problem
might become bigger.

261
00:12:00,433 --> 00:12:01,833
I already took care of it,
Isobel.

262
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:06,400
I'm going to teach
Salvador a lesson.

263
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:09,400
Oh, no.
Ricardo, don't do that.

264
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:14,467
If you do, then your plan
might become a bigger issue.

265
00:12:14,667 --> 00:12:16,667
Whatever happens to him...

266
00:12:16,833 --> 00:12:18,467
happened because
he asked for it!

267
00:12:19,067 --> 00:12:21,633
Let this serve as a lesson
to the media industry

268
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:24,200
to think before they attack me.

269
00:12:24,333 --> 00:12:29,700
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

270
00:12:29,833 --> 00:12:32,600
Families like that
are really something.

271
00:12:34,367 --> 00:12:36,333
- They're money-hungry.
- [UMALI] Jacinto!

272
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:37,800
[SIGHS]

273
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,533
- [MAX] Sir.
- [CHUCKLES]

274
00:12:42,667 --> 00:12:45,133
Why aren't you wearing
your uniform?

275
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:46,467
Are you off duty?

276
00:12:46,633 --> 00:12:48,800
Oh, we went to Ginintuang Lupa.

277
00:12:48,933 --> 00:12:54,567
Colonel Domingo asked us
to sort out something.

278
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:58,833
You went to Ginintuang Lupa
without telling me?

279
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,667
I could've gone with you

280
00:13:00,767 --> 00:13:04,167
so we could protect
the police station's princess!

281
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:07,833
Princess?

282
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:11,067
Sir, I am a cop.

283
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:13,500
I can protect myself.

284
00:13:14,567 --> 00:13:17,500
Ah, you're wearing civilian
clothes too, sir.

285
00:13:17,667 --> 00:13:18,500
Where are you going?

286
00:13:18,667 --> 00:13:20,633
Oh, it's nothing.

287
00:13:20,733 --> 00:13:22,733
- Just a routine check.
- Here.

288
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:24,667
Have you seen this?

289
00:13:26,033 --> 00:13:29,700
[SALVADOR]<i> General
</i> Ricardo Jacinto!

290
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:33,200
Will you finally stop bothering
the people in Ginintuang Lupa?

291
00:13:34,067 --> 00:13:36,233
<i>Or are you just
clearing your head?</i>

292
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:38,733
- [MAX] That's slander!
- Law enforcers!

293
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:41,367
Just because he stands
with the poor

294
00:13:41,533 --> 00:13:44,267
doesn't mean he can paint
my father as the villain.

295
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:46,333
Don't be stressed.

296
00:13:46,433 --> 00:13:48,600
Let's let this situation
cool down first.

297
00:13:48,733 --> 00:13:50,333
He'll eventually stop babbling.

298
00:13:50,433 --> 00:13:55,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

299
00:13:55,467 --> 00:13:56,900
Excuse me, sir.

300
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:58,733
[ESTRELLA] Excuse me.

301
00:14:03,133 --> 00:14:04,067
Here.

302
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:07,200
[PAQUITO] Come eat with me.

303
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:08,767
I don't want to.
I'm still full.

304
00:14:08,933 --> 00:14:11,200
Are you still jealous
of Betchay, Ibyang?

305
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:13,733
Why would I be jealous?

306
00:14:13,833 --> 00:14:18,633
I'm obviously younger
and more beautiful than her!

307
00:14:18,767 --> 00:14:21,433
Paquito won't leave you
over Betchay!

308
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:22,733
He better not!

309
00:14:22,833 --> 00:14:25,700
Let me remind you, Paquito.

310
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:28,267
I have made a lot
of sacrifices in this business.

311
00:14:28,467 --> 00:14:30,933
And you'll just let
Betchay work there?

312
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:34,900
Their family is the plague
to our business!

313
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:35,933
Ibyang.

314
00:14:36,033 --> 00:14:39,100
How many times
do I have to explain

315
00:14:39,267 --> 00:14:42,567
that Betchay is useful?

316
00:14:42,667 --> 00:14:45,833
I'll use her against
Rudy and Gabo.

317
00:14:45,967 --> 00:14:48,467
- So we can finally beat them.
- Oh gosh!

318
00:14:48,633 --> 00:14:52,500
I want that woman
out of BeerGin!

319
00:14:52,633 --> 00:14:54,333
I don't want her to work there!

320
00:14:54,467 --> 00:14:55,767
I'll think about it.

321
00:14:55,933 --> 00:14:59,233
What do you mean?
It's a very easy decision!

322
00:15:00,033 --> 00:15:01,567
[OBJECTS CLATTERS]

323
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:03,533
[ROMY] Here's my advice,
brother.

324
00:15:03,667 --> 00:15:05,833
- Go ahead.
- Listen to her or you might...

325
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,700
Well... Betchay
still has some sex appeal.

326
00:15:10,833 --> 00:15:12,300
[ROMY] Here's what
I'm curious about, Paquito.

327
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:15,200
Out of all the places
to apply from,

328
00:15:15,333 --> 00:15:17,833
- she decided on BeerGin.
- Well...

329
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,367
She's desperate.
She had no other choice.

330
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:22,800
[ROMY] What's the update
on Rudy?

331
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:25,433
I heard he's
in critical condition.

332
00:15:25,533 --> 00:15:27,100
He hasn't woken up until now.

333
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:30,833
If I were Betchay,
I'd give up on Rudy.

334
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:35,600
Look at her now.
She'll be in so much dept

335
00:15:35,733 --> 00:15:37,900
and then what?
He dies anyway.

336
00:15:38,033 --> 00:15:40,000
- Tell me, am I wrong?
- [KNIFE CLATTERS]

337
00:15:40,167 --> 00:15:41,000
It's the truth.

338
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:43,300
Let me tell you this,

339
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:45,167
with poor people like us,

340
00:15:45,333 --> 00:15:46,567
when one of us gets sick,

341
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:50,800
that means only
a 50% chance of surviving.

342
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:53,233
And then we die eventually.

343
00:15:53,367 --> 00:15:54,700
Am I right?

344
00:15:54,867 --> 00:15:57,667
Why do you seem
so concerned about Betchay?

345
00:15:57,833 --> 00:15:59,333
Oh please, Ibyang,

346
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:02,367
quit nagging.

347
00:16:02,533 --> 00:16:03,800
Don't make me angry.

348
00:16:04,933 --> 00:16:05,967
What?

349
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:10,000
Hey, are you trying to kill me
with that much chili?

350
00:16:11,067 --> 00:16:11,933
That's too much.

351
00:16:12,067 --> 00:16:13,333
I hope it makes
your stomach hurt.

352
00:16:15,233 --> 00:16:17,200
- She still got it, right?
- Definitely.

353
00:16:17,367 --> 00:16:18,700
I'm still here, you know!

354
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:20,367
I can hear you!

355
00:16:20,467 --> 00:16:22,667
Hey, we're just kidding!

356
00:16:22,767 --> 00:16:24,033
[PLATE CLANKS]

357
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:27,900
[KID] Boss Django! Boss Django!

358
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:30,667
Here's all we got.

359
00:16:30,767 --> 00:16:32,533
- Give it to Udo. Udo!
- [UDO] Come here.

360
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,033
[BOTTLES CLINK]

361
00:16:34,133 --> 00:16:35,067
Boss Django,

362
00:16:36,367 --> 00:16:37,867
these are our recruits.

363
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:40,600
Where did you find those?

364
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:43,600
At the dump yard.
They're new in the area.

365
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,967
[LIQUID TRICKLES]

366
00:16:46,333 --> 00:16:47,233
[SPLAT]

367
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:55,733
What are your names?

368
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:57,700
- I'm Boybits, boss.
- I'm Pulong.

369
00:16:57,800 --> 00:16:59,067
I'm Kanor, boss.

370
00:16:59,167 --> 00:17:00,433
I'm Ador, boss.

371
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:01,633
I'm Hector, boss.

372
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,367
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

373
00:17:05,467 --> 00:17:07,067
Are you guys good at fighting?

374
00:17:07,233 --> 00:17:08,633
They're great, boss.

375
00:17:08,767 --> 00:17:10,433
They're used to
neighborhood fights.

376
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:12,033
I didn't ask you.

377
00:17:12,133 --> 00:17:15,933
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [MEN GRUNTING]

378
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:20,000
[GUN COCKS]

379
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,600
[MUSIC TURNS SOMBER]

380
00:17:24,700 --> 00:17:27,000
[LAUGHS MOCKINGLY]

381
00:17:28,333 --> 00:17:29,300
That's what I'm looking for.

382
00:17:30,133 --> 00:17:31,233
Someone strong.

383
00:17:33,767 --> 00:17:34,933
Listen up.

384
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:38,400
We have a few rules around here.

385
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:40,167
First,

386
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:43,933
you must obey all of my orders.

387
00:17:44,533 --> 00:17:46,067
And my Pa's too, Paquito.

388
00:17:47,433 --> 00:17:48,400
We are the bosses here.

389
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:50,533
Second,

390
00:17:51,033 --> 00:17:53,467
you need to put money
on the table.

391
00:17:53,567 --> 00:17:55,667
I don't care how you do it.

392
00:17:56,467 --> 00:17:59,167
What matters is that
you keep money coming in here.

393
00:17:59,333 --> 00:18:00,300
Do you understand?!

394
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:01,433
- Yes, boss!
- Yes, boss!

395
00:18:03,733 --> 00:18:04,967
Good.

396
00:18:07,667 --> 00:18:08,833
Boss Paquito.

397
00:18:13,567 --> 00:18:15,667
- Pa.
- Oh, Django.

398
00:18:17,333 --> 00:18:18,667
These are our recruits.

399
00:18:18,833 --> 00:18:20,000
They're strong.

400
00:18:20,167 --> 00:18:23,033
We can use them in operations
while Topak is in jail.

401
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:25,733
Aside from being strong
and brave,

402
00:18:26,367 --> 00:18:29,967
you must also
do the job cleanly.

403
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:33,300
We don't want to get in trouble.
Do you understand?

404
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:34,467
- Yes, boss!
- Yes, boss!

405
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:36,700
I got this, Pa.

406
00:18:36,867 --> 00:18:38,067
I'll train them.

407
00:18:38,667 --> 00:18:40,367
I'll let them tag along with me.

408
00:18:40,533 --> 00:18:42,667
Alright. That's good, Django.

409
00:18:42,833 --> 00:18:44,500
Get your men ready,

410
00:18:44,667 --> 00:18:46,967
so when you cross paths
with Gabo,

411
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:49,167
we won't lose again.

412
00:18:49,333 --> 00:18:53,867
[PHONE RINGING]

413
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:57,200
- Hello?
- Let's meet in your area.

414
00:18:59,367 --> 00:19:00,333
Where?

415
00:19:00,433 --> 00:19:01,767
Where do we always meet?

416
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:03,567
Do I need to remind you
where it is?

417
00:19:03,733 --> 00:19:04,567
The usual spot!

418
00:19:04,733 --> 00:19:05,833
<i> Hurry up!</i>

419
00:19:05,933 --> 00:19:07,333
I'm on my way.

420
00:19:09,967 --> 00:19:12,167
Umali wants to talk to us.

421
00:19:12,267 --> 00:19:13,067
Why?

422
00:19:13,067 --> 00:19:15,867
He didn't say,
but it seems important.

423
00:19:16,100 --> 00:19:19,167
Come on. Let's not make
our guest wait.

424
00:19:21,233 --> 00:19:22,200
Give me my shirt.

425
00:19:22,367 --> 00:19:29,167
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

426
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:38,267
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

427
00:19:38,267 --> 00:19:40,667
This guy's name is Umali.

428
00:19:40,667 --> 00:19:43,567
He's the one
who gives us jobs.

429
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:49,233
[PAQUITO CLEARS THROAT]

430
00:19:58,733 --> 00:19:59,933
They're here.

431
00:20:08,133 --> 00:20:11,300
[SNICKERS] You've got some nerve
to come here, don't you think?

432
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:15,133
Did you forget you're part
of the demolition team?!

433
00:20:15,133 --> 00:20:16,300
Django.

434
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:17,567
Calm down.

435
00:20:18,367 --> 00:20:21,167
Let's listen
to what they have to say.

436
00:20:21,167 --> 00:20:24,133
So that's what
you're angry about, Django.

437
00:20:24,133 --> 00:20:26,133
That's it? Did the demolition
go as planned?

438
00:20:26,133 --> 00:20:27,800
Not for now!

439
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:29,133
And then what?!

440
00:20:29,133 --> 00:20:31,433
You're thinking far ahead.

441
00:20:31,433 --> 00:20:32,800
Don't worry about it for now.

442
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:34,333
I'm not thinking far ahead!

443
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,533
I just want to know now...

444
00:20:37,167 --> 00:20:39,467
what side you're choosing
when all hell breaks loose.

445
00:20:40,167 --> 00:20:42,167
Is it with your bosses,
the higher-ups,

446
00:20:42,167 --> 00:20:44,600
or with us who brings you money?

447
00:20:47,667 --> 00:20:49,200
Django.

448
00:20:50,033 --> 00:20:52,633
We'll side with those
who we can benefit more from.

449
00:20:52,633 --> 00:20:54,033
Do you understand?

450
00:20:55,467 --> 00:20:57,167
Umali...

451
00:20:57,167 --> 00:21:00,667
If that unfortunate day
happens again,

452
00:21:00,667 --> 00:21:03,167
I hope we all do
the right thing.

453
00:21:03,167 --> 00:21:06,467
We don't want
to blame each other in the end.

454
00:21:06,467 --> 00:21:10,100
And why did you ask us
to come here?

455
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:16,200
The keywords
are cool and mainstream.

456
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:17,700
- Boss, boss.
- Oh, Salvador.

457
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:18,833
You're here.

458
00:21:18,833 --> 00:21:20,200
What's going on, boss?

459
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:21,333
Oh, come on!

460
00:21:21,333 --> 00:21:25,667
In an hour, we'll do a look test
for your makeover.

461
00:21:25,667 --> 00:21:27,733
Salvador, you're a big shot now!

462
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:30,833
They hired a whole team
for your makeover!

463
00:21:30,833 --> 00:21:32,400
That's fantastic, man!

464
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,367
For what?

465
00:21:33,367 --> 00:21:35,600
For your new show!

466
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:37,333
Goodness. Just go.

467
00:21:38,367 --> 00:21:41,433
Makeup! Makeup, Salvador!
Come on, sit. Sit down.

468
00:21:41,433 --> 00:21:42,400
Hold on.

469
00:21:42,433 --> 00:21:43,800
[SPRITZING]

470
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:45,400
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

471
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:47,600
Wow! Man, you look good!

472
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:50,867
That's bitter.

473
00:21:51,867 --> 00:21:53,167
Wear these.

474
00:21:56,267 --> 00:22:03,233
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

475
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:09,867
Salvador!

476
00:22:09,867 --> 00:22:10,933
[CHUCKLES, CLAPS]

477
00:22:10,933 --> 00:22:14,733
What does it feel like
to be a star?

478
00:22:14,733 --> 00:22:16,400
Tell me, man,
are you having fun?

479
00:22:16,433 --> 00:22:18,233
I'm still a reporter.

480
00:22:18,233 --> 00:22:19,567
I'm just wearing fancy clothes.

481
00:22:19,567 --> 00:22:21,167
If anything, I'm a starlet.

482
00:22:21,167 --> 00:22:23,900
Whether it be
a starlet, starfish,

483
00:22:23,900 --> 00:22:27,567
or star apple,
you're still a star, man.

484
00:22:28,900 --> 00:22:32,267
You've always been this way,
doubting yourself.

485
00:22:32,267 --> 00:22:33,600
Do you see all of that?

486
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:36,667
That's all for you, man.

487
00:22:36,667 --> 00:22:39,867
If you think
you don't have potential,

488
00:22:41,633 --> 00:22:43,400
then why did they bother
doing all of this?

489
00:22:44,433 --> 00:22:45,533
Well, you're right.

490
00:22:46,900 --> 00:22:48,533
It's nice...

491
00:22:49,333 --> 00:22:51,267
to know that the stories
you tell matter.

492
00:22:51,267 --> 00:22:54,900
[CHUCKLES] Of course.
We're partners, remember?

493
00:22:58,167 --> 00:22:59,433
I have a job for you.

494
00:22:59,433 --> 00:23:02,800
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

495
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:03,800
[PAPER RUSTLES]

496
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:04,767
Hmm.

497
00:23:06,933 --> 00:23:07,900
Just like before?

498
00:23:08,867 --> 00:23:09,900
You want him killed?

499
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:11,933
Not really.

500
00:23:11,933 --> 00:23:13,267
Just scare him.

501
00:23:14,167 --> 00:23:16,600
Let's just kill him.
It'd be easier.

502
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:17,767
Don't.

503
00:23:18,933 --> 00:23:21,200
That reporter
always targets our station.

504
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:22,933
We're always in his news scoop.

505
00:23:22,967 --> 00:23:27,000
He thinks we shot the man
during the demolition.

506
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
If something happens to him,

507
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:32,200
they'll suspect no one but us.

508
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:36,567
You could make it look like
a robbery incident.

509
00:23:36,567 --> 00:23:39,000
He fought back
that's why he got beaten up.

510
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,233
Or stabbed.

511
00:23:40,233 --> 00:23:41,900
Or it could be...

512
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:43,500
he got shot.

513
00:23:43,500 --> 00:23:44,967
But don't shoot him dead.

514
00:23:44,967 --> 00:23:46,967
The goal is to keep

515
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:52,467
that bastard's mouth shut.

516
00:23:54,633 --> 00:23:55,800
Here's the downpayment.

517
00:23:55,833 --> 00:24:01,533
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

518
00:24:01,533 --> 00:24:04,900
Make sure
to get the job done cleanly.

519
00:24:04,900 --> 00:24:06,633
Of course. [SNICKERS]

520
00:24:07,867 --> 00:24:09,367
You've got it, Umali.

521
00:24:10,600 --> 00:24:12,300
We'll take care of this.

522
00:24:14,867 --> 00:24:21,800
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

523
00:24:25,067 --> 00:24:31,500
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

524
00:24:34,633 --> 00:24:37,233
Uncle, how is Papa?

525
00:24:37,367 --> 00:24:39,000
Still the same.

526
00:24:39,133 --> 00:24:40,767
Have you seen the bike?

527
00:24:41,467 --> 00:24:42,500
It would be a waste
if you lost that.

528
00:24:42,633 --> 00:24:44,867
What now, Gabo?
Didn't you promise

529
00:24:44,967 --> 00:24:46,933
that you're going to
solve that problem?

530
00:24:47,100 --> 00:24:48,100
Don't worry.

531
00:24:49,033 --> 00:24:50,367
I got the bike.

532
00:24:50,467 --> 00:24:52,767
Oh, that's a relief.

533
00:24:52,900 --> 00:24:56,367
The owner can reclaim
their bike.

534
00:24:56,467 --> 00:24:59,033
Rudy can finally
undergo surgery.

535
00:24:59,467 --> 00:25:00,900
Finally,

536
00:25:01,033 --> 00:25:02,833
you have some good news for us.

537
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:06,067
A break from all the problems
you've caused us.

538
00:25:06,167 --> 00:25:08,733
[MAMENG] Oh my gosh, Betchay.
Come on, Betchay.

539
00:25:08,833 --> 00:25:12,800
I wonder if there
will ever be a day

540
00:25:12,933 --> 00:25:16,033
when I'll get to say that
you're not being a buzzkill.

541
00:25:16,167 --> 00:25:17,433
How is it my fault again?

542
00:25:17,567 --> 00:25:18,467
- Just shush.
- That's enough.

543
00:25:18,633 --> 00:25:20,633
You're giving me a headache.
Go on, Gabo.

544
00:25:20,767 --> 00:25:22,867
Go see your father.

545
00:25:24,900 --> 00:25:31,800
- [EKG MACHINE BEEPING]
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

546
00:25:46,933 --> 00:25:48,900
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [BEEPING CONTINUES]

547
00:25:49,033 --> 00:25:53,900
- [EKG BEEPING RAPIDLY]
- [RUDY GRUNTING]

548
00:25:59,033 --> 00:26:00,733
Pa! Pa!

549
00:26:00,867 --> 00:26:03,633
Doc! Doc, help! Help!

550
00:26:04,633 --> 00:26:05,833
Pa...

551
00:26:06,367 --> 00:26:07,733
Pa! Pa!

552
00:26:07,867 --> 00:26:09,300
- Excuse me, sir.
- Pa! Pa!

553
00:26:09,467 --> 00:26:12,167
- Rudy! Rudy! Rudy!
- Pa. Pa! Pa!

554
00:26:12,300 --> 00:26:14,633
Doc, please do everything
to save my father!

555
00:26:14,733 --> 00:26:16,700
- [BETCHAY SOBBING]
- Pa! Pa!

556
00:26:16,833 --> 00:26:19,267
- Gabo! What happened?!
- Pa! Pa...

557
00:26:19,700 --> 00:26:21,033
- Rudy!
- Pa!

558
00:26:21,167 --> 00:26:22,200
Pa!

559
00:26:23,233 --> 00:26:24,167
Pa!

560
00:26:25,633 --> 00:26:26,800
[MAMENG] Gabo, come here!

561
00:26:27,400 --> 00:26:29,100
Pa! Pa!

562
00:26:29,233 --> 00:26:34,167
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

563
00:26:34,300 --> 00:26:35,200
Pa!

564
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:57,400
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

565
00:27:01,067 --> 00:27:02,900
<i> He should find a way</i>

566
00:27:03,033 --> 00:27:06,533
to help save his father's life.

567
00:27:06,667 --> 00:27:07,733
<i> What do you need, Gabo?</i>

568
00:27:07,867 --> 00:27:08,800
<i> Please help me.</i>

569
00:27:08,900 --> 00:27:10,133
<i> I need money.</i>

570
00:27:10,233 --> 00:27:12,167
<i>If we don't move now,
we won't have another chance.</i>

571
00:27:12,333 --> 00:27:13,500
This case is personal to me now.

572
00:27:13,667 --> 00:27:16,633
<i>I'm not going to stop until
Tiger is held accountable.</i>

573
00:27:16,767 --> 00:27:18,267
<i> That's Samantha Jacinto.</i>

574
00:27:18,400 --> 00:27:19,767
<i>She was the one who arrested
my brother.</i>

575
00:27:19,900 --> 00:27:22,000
<i> I'll take care of her myself.</i>

576
00:27:22,100 --> 00:27:23,933
<i>There are a lot of eyes
watching us.</i>

577
00:27:24,067 --> 00:27:26,033
<i>We need to be careful
so our plan won't fail.</i>

578
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:27,500
<i> I know that you need my help</i>

579
00:27:27,600 --> 00:27:30,267
<i>because your father
is in the hospital</i>

580
00:27:30,400 --> 00:27:32,033
and is in a critical condition.

581
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:34,333
<i> You need to get the gold</i>

582
00:27:34,467 --> 00:27:37,167
<i>from Mr. Chan,
whether he's dead or alive.</i>

583
00:27:37,267 --> 00:27:38,200
<i> We will arrest Mr. Chan.</i>

584
00:27:38,367 --> 00:27:40,000
<i>This time, we won't let him
get away.</i>
